      ("Reviews, photos and consent",
       "<p>Reviews matter more in aesthetics than in most industries because the result is visible. Ask satisfied clients to review you on the platforms they already use and reply without sharing personal details. Before-and-after photos are powerful but need written consent, consistent lighting and honest captions. Never edit results, and avoid promising outcomes; aesthetic results vary and medical advertising rules in most states prohibit misleading claims.</p>"),
      ("Content ideas beyond treatment pages",
       "<p>Seasonal and decision content performs well: how far ahead of a wedding to book treatments, what to avoid before and after an appointment, how to choose between two similar treatments, how to spot an unqualified provider. Each piece should link to the matching treatment page and be reviewed by a clinician. Content like this answers the follow-up questions AI tools look for when building a complete answer.</p>"),
